    "vipSummary": {
      "id": 1448744769,
      "html": "<p>CYP2C19 is one of the key pharmacogenes involved in implementation of pharmacogenomics.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>It is involved in guidelines for antidepressants, <a href=\"/chemical/PA449053/guidelineAnnotation/PA166104948\">clopidogrel</a> and <a href=\"/chemical/PA10233/guidelineAnnotation/PA166161537\">voriconazole</a> (<a href=\"/gene/PA124/prescribingInfo\">go to list of all guidelines with CYP2C19</a>).</li>\n<li>the nomenclature has been set by <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.pharmvar.org/gene/CYP2C19\" target=\"_blank\">PharmVar</a>, note that the reference sequence for CYP2C19 on hg38 is equivalent to <a href=\"/haplotype/PA166218473\">CYP2C19*38</a> not <a href=\"/haplotype/PA165980634\">CYP2C19*1</a>.</li>\n<li>the AMP tier 1 alleles are <a href=\"/haplotype/PA165980635\">CYP2C19*2</a>, <a href=\"/haplotype/PA165980636\">CYP2C19*3</a> and <a href=\"/haplotype/PA165816533\">CYP2C19*17</a> <a href=\"/ampAllelesToTest\">see all alleles on the AMP recommended to test list</a></li>\n<li>key variant pages are <a href=\"/variant/PA166154053\">rs4244285</a>(part of *2),  <a href=\"/variant/PA166154070\">rs4986893</a>(part of *3) and <a href=\"/variant/PA166154147\">rs12248560</a>(part of *17)</li>\n<li>See the <a href=\"/page/cyp2c19RefMaterials\">Gene-specific Information Tables</a> for Allele Definitions (for which variants comprise which star alleles), Allele function assignments (normal function, no function, decreased or increased function etc) and Diplotype-Phenotype Table (for how the alleles combine to form metabolizer phenotypes for PM, NM, UM)</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
